  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing - `POST /upload` returns 500.\n\nEvidence used (11/12 checks):\n\n* App + DB both `running` - `incidentlab-app-1 Up 5 seconds`, `incidentlab-db-1 Up 10 seconds (healthy)` (E1). Confirmed in detail: app `running:true, exit_code:0, oom_killed:false` (E8), db `running:true, exit_code:0, oom_killed:false, health:healthy` (E11).\n* App `/health` returns `200 {\"status\":\"ok\"}` (E2). App logs also show `GET /health 200 OK` continuing after upload failures (E4).\n* Recent restarts seen in last 60m: `kill/stop/die/destroy/rename/start` for both containers (E3), but currently running per E1,E8,E11.\n* App logs show initial success then failure (E4):\n  `POST /upload 200 OK` x2, `GET /files/... 200 OK`, `DELETE ... 200 OK` x2, then\n  `POST /upload 500 Internal Server Error` +\n  `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/e10bcb4ef703fe1a8d4d66a9403555e8.part'` at `File \"/app/main.py\", line 55, in upload` in `with open(tmp_path, \"wb\") as out:`\n* DB logs show no error: `database system is ready to accept connections` (E5), `Skipping initialization` (E5).\n* Host filesystem `/srv/lab-data` has space: `use_percent:9.0, available_mb:410.6, inode_use_percent:0.2` (E6). Root `/` also has space: `use_percent:6.8, inode_use_percent:1.5` (E10). Rules out disk-full / inode-full.\n* Bind mount: `source:/srv/lab-data destination:/data rw:true` (E8), app user `1000:1000` (E8). Therefore container `/data/tmp/...part` = host `/srv/lab-data/tmp/...part`.\n* Parent dirs themselves are writable: `/srv/lab-data/uploads is_dir:true owner 1000:1000 mode 0755 app_user_can_write:true` (E7), `/srv/lab-data is_dir:true owner 1000:1000 mode 0755 app_user_can_write:true` (E9).\n\nConclusion:\n\nRoot cause: Application cannot write temp file for upload - `PermissionError Errno 13` on `/data/tmp/*.part` in `upload` (E4). This is direct evidence of the cause itself, not inferred by elimination.\n\nSymptoms vs cause:\n* Symptom is `POST /upload 500` (E4). Health still `200` (E2,E4) and containers `running` (E1,E8,E11), so not a crash / down container.\n* Dependency DB is not the cause: `healthy` (E1,E11) + ready for connections (E5).\n* Disk/inode full is not the cause: 9.0% and 6.8% used (E6,E10).\n* Top-level `uploads` dir permission is not the cause: writable (E7). Parent also writable (E9). Failure is in `tmp` sub-path (E4,E8).\n\nLimitation: `path_access` tool only covers `/srv/lab-data` (E9) and `/srv/lab-data/uploads` (E7). Exact owner/mode of `/srv/lab-data/tmp` was not observed, so do not assume its value. Repair (chown/chmod/investigate tmp) requires human approval - no changes made.\n",
